    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** leading the charge, boasting an elite 85.94 score. His matchup against Chandler is a primary target for our stolen base strategy; despite the catcher\u2019s 1.86s pop time, the combination of Chandler\u2019s slow delivery and a favorable wind direction maximizes the efficiency for our speed-first approach. **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.94) round out our top-tier outfield options. **Mickey Moniak** specifically benefits from a significant 14% platoon boost against King, while **James Wood** continues to leverage his elite 0.425 xwOBA to punish a vulnerable starter in a hitter-friendly environment. We are also capitalizing on the high-floor production of **Gabriel Moreno** (71.17), whose pairing against the soft-tossing Chandler makes him a premium play at C2.\n\nOur decision-making process was most tested at the MI/Utility slots, where **Brice Turang** (63.87) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (62.65) secured starts over high-effort but lower-efficiency alternatives. The most difficult cut was **Travis Bazzana**, who landed at 41.56; while his park factor was positive, the harsh L/L platoon disadvantage against Ferguson made him the clear odd man out compared to the reliable daily output of **Vinnie Pasquantino**. Risks remain, notably with **Isaac Paredes** (43.49), whose start is tenuous given his negative SP skill and platoon splits against Detmers; he remains in the lineup only due to a lack of better utility depth. Meanwhile, **Dalton Rushing** is flirting with the floor at 50.34, hampered primarily by his #9 spot in the order, though his recent form keeps him just clear of the benching threshold. We continue to monitor the status of **Trevor Story** and **Jose Caballero**, neither of whom provides utility today as we navigate the roster.",
